To compute the infinite sum \(\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{F_{n + 1}}{F_n F_{n + 2}}\), where \(F_n\) denotes the \(n\)th Fibonacci number, we start by examining the series and using properties of Fibonacci numbers.

First, we compute the partial sums to observe any patterns:
