\( (\cos a - \cos b)^2 + (\sin a - \sin b)^2 = 2 - 2 \cos(a - b) \)

Using the identity \( (\cos x - \cos y)^2 + (\sin x - \sin y)^2 = 2 - 2 \cos(x - y) \).

So, \( a - b = \pi/16 - 9\pi/16 = -8\pi/16 = -\pi/2 \). So, \( \cos(a - b) = \cos(-\pi/2) = 0 \).

Thus, the expression becomes \( 2 - 2 \times 0 = 2 \).

Therefore, \( |z_1 - z_2|^2 = 2^{1/4} \times 2 = 2^{5/4} \).

So, the distance between \( z_1 \) and \( z_2 \) is \( \sqrt{2^{5/4}} = 2^{5/8} \).

Therefore, the side length is \( 2^{5/8} \), so area is \( (2^{5/8})^2 = 2^{5/4} \).

Hence, the area is \( 2^{5/4} \), so in the form \( p^{a/b} \), \( p = 2 \), \( a = 5 \), \( b = 4 \), so \( a + b + p = 5 + 4 + 2 = 11 \).

