First, convert 2.5 hours to seconds:
\[ 2.5 \text{ hours} = 2.5 \times 60 \times 60 = 9000 \text{ seconds} \]

The robot's speed is:
\[ \text{Speed} = \frac{1 \text{ km}}{9000 \text{ seconds}} = \frac{1000 \text{ meters}}{9000 \text{ seconds}} = \frac{1}{9} \text{ meters per second} \]

Next, calculate the distance traveled in 90 seconds:
\[ \text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time} = \frac{1}{9} \text{ m/s} \times 90 \text{ s} = 10 \text{ meters} \]

Thus, the length of the hallway is:
\[ \boxed{10} \]
