To convert the bicycle's speed from feet per minute to inches per second, we follow these steps:

1. Start with the given speed: 20 feet per minute.
2. Convert feet to inches: 
   \[
   20 \text{ feet per minute} \times 12 \text{ inches per foot} = 240 \text{ inches per minute}
   \]
3. Convert minutes to seconds by dividing by 60:
   \[
   240 \text{ inches per minute} \div 60 \text{ seconds per minute} = 4 \text{ inches per second}
   \]

Thus, the bicycle's speed is \(\boxed{4}\) inches per second.
