   \[
   \text{Euros} = \frac{150}{1.32} \approx 113.64
   \]

Next, we find the difference between the number of euros and pounds:
\[
113.64 - 91.46 = 22.18
\]

Rounding 22.18 to the nearest whole number gives 22.

Thus, Kathy will have \boxed{22} more euros than pounds. 72%|███████▏  | 286/400 [6:02:58<3:01:25, 95.48s/it]  72%|███████▏  | 287/400 [6:03:24<2:20:29, 74.60s/it]
