2. Calculate the gasoline used by the hybrid car:
   \[
   \text{Gasoline used by hybrid} = \frac{\text{Total miles driven}}{\text{Miles per gallon (mpg)}} = \frac{12,000 \text{ miles}}{48 \text{ mpg}} = 250 \text{ gallons}
   \]

3. Find the difference in gasoline usage:
   \[
   \text{Savings} = \text{Gasoline used by SUV} - \text{Gasoline used by hybrid} = 800 \text{ gallons} - 250 \text{ gallons} = 550 \text{ gallons}
   \]

Thus, the amount of gasoline Karla would have saved last year is \boxed{550} gallons.
