Given the polynomial equation:

\[ z^8 - z^7 + z^6 - z^5 + z^4 - z^3 + z^2 - z + 1 = 0 \]

we recognize that it can be written as:

\[ \frac{z^9 + 1}{z + 1} = 0 \]

This implies that the roots are the 9th roots of -1, excluding \( z = -1 \). The roots are the solutions to \( z^9 = -1 \), which are the 18th roots of unity at odd multiples of \( \pi/9 \). These roots are:

\[ z = e^{i\pi(2k + 1)/9} \quad \text{for} \quad k = 0, 1, 2, \ldots, 8 \]

excluding \( z = -1 \) (which corresponds to \( k = 4 \)). Therefore, the roots are:

\[ z = e^{i\pi/9}, e^{i3\pi/9}, e^{i5\pi/9}, e^{i7\pi/9}, e^{i11\pi/9}, e^{i13\pi/9}, e^{i15\pi/9}, e^{i17\pi/9} \]

These correspond to the angles:

